    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1417">

                <pb facs="1248" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg990"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1317</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Marye</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 30, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. German Embassy informs Department safe-conducts taken from Germans captured
                    on Persian territory by Russians at RussoPersian border, male German prisoners
                    made spend nine days in jail with highwaymen at Nakhichevan. The male Germans
                    found Tabriz sent to Astrakhan prisoners of war.</p>
                <p>Bring to attention Foreign Office and do what you properly can behalf Germans
                    imprisoned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
